{"from": "text:4q521-2", "to": "claim:lk-04-18-isaiah-61-quoted", "type": "attests", "grade": "C", "note": "4Q521, a pre-Christian Qumran text, expects God's agent to 'proclaim good news to the poor... freeing prisoners, giving sight to the blind' - the same Isaianic liberation cluster as Luke 4:18 already applied to an eschatological figure in Judaism before Jesus. It attests the currency of that hope, not that Jesus read Isaiah 61 in Nazareth."}
